Z||000008||Kelvin Vivian||04-23-2001||02:12 PM||||Here are pics of a GT and a notchback which show the stock locations of the spoiler. I've noticed that on the notchback, it appears that the wing is set further to the rear. <P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402876&Sequence=3&res=high"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402878&Sequence=3&res=high"> <P>I think setting the wing back on the GT would look good.||||reg||1
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||04-23-2001||03:24 PM||||I think that moving the spoiler back lengthens the GT out nicely. In the Witzenberg's book Fiero on page 89 (I wish I had a scanner) there is a notchback with the spoiler pushed back to make room for the overroof snorkel. You can see how the extensions drop down the side of the trunk lid. I think it would be a good idea and very subtle!||||reg||14
